+| S-6 | medium | `security/redact.ts` ≈132 `redactSensitiveText` | Pattern-only; never calls `security/detect/entropy.ts`. Opaque bearer tokens and bare hex keys in tool output reach the model unredacted. This is the one scrubber on every tool output (`agent.ts` ≈3337) and on web content. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC2): `redactSensitiveText` now also runs `detectEntropy`, masking a qualifying match as `[REDACTED:entropy]`; `entropy.ts` gained allow-shapes (40-hex git SHA, UUID, npm/yarn `sha256-`/`sha512-` integrity) so ordinary command output is not a false positive. **Review round (PR #776) found and fixed three more defects here**: F-LOG-F1 (blocker) — `TOKEN`'s `/` meant a URL's `host/path/…/<sha40>` was one joined run, escaping the allow-shapes AND picking up a false label from an "api." hostname substring; URLs are now decomposed (host excluded, each path segment/query value/fragment scanned separately, label-free) and the generic per-line scan skips any span inside a recognised URL. F-SEC-F2 (major) — an allow-shape used to exempt a value even with an adjacent explicit label (`'leaked token: <sha>'` stayed unredacted); the per-line scan no longer consults the allow-shape at all once a label is required and found. F-REG-F3 (major, shared with S-9) — `HEX_BLOB` accepted digits-only runs; `isHexBlob` now also requires an a–f letter (a base-10 alphabet cannot reach the 3.6-bit floor at any length, so this closes the gap rather than narrowing it) — see S-9 for the SAME fix's `displayUrl` test, and separately, `redactSensitiveText`/`containsOutboundSecret` now honour `backends.entropy.enabled` via `security/entropy-gate.ts` (F-REG-F3's config-gate half). F-LOG-F2 (minor) — dead `SHORT_GIT_SHA_RE` removed (entropy is bounded by log2(N); nothing under 13 characters can ever qualify). Tests: `redact.test.ts` ("S-6 …", "F-SEC-F2 …", "F-LOG-F1 …", "F-REG-F3 …"), `entropy.test.ts` (same four groups plus `looksSecretShaped`), `redact.false-positive-fixture.test.ts` (204-sample fixture — grown from 200 with the two F-LOG-F1 URLs, a GitHub raw URL and an npm tarball+integrity-query URL — false-positive count 0; a companion test pins a signed S3 URL's `X-Amz-Signature` as a documented TRUE positive, since a presigned-URL signature is a live credential). **Review round 2 found the F-LOG-F1 fix was incomplete**: a `+`-joined multi-word search query (`q=bun+test+timeout+flaky`, literally `web_search`'s own wire shape) was still one non-slug entropy-eligible run (`+` sits inside `TOKEN`'s class; `isWordSlug` never split on it), and a versioned package filename (`typescript-5.6.3.tgz`) was still redacted whenever its dot-free remainder reached 20+ characters. Fixed with one shared primitive, `secretShapedCandidatesIn`/`looksSecretShapedIn`: `+` is swapped for a literal space (length-preserving) before re-tokenising a URL component, and `isWordSlug` now accepts a segment that transitions at most once between a letter-run and a digit-run (`cp311`, `x86`, `manylinux_2_17` — a Python wheel filename's platform tags) as structured rather than random, closing a SEPARATE false positive (`numpy-1.26.4-cp311-cp311-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl`) found while building the round-2 fixture. `outbound-secret.ts` now calls this SAME shared function instead of its own duplicate check. Tests: `redact.test.ts`/`outbound-secret.test.ts` "BOUNDARY (review round 2) …" (the two exact reported URLs), `entropy.test.ts` (the wheel-filename case), `outbound-secret.ordinary-fixture.test.ts` (new — 65 realistic URLs/queries across search/npm/PyPI/crates/GitHub/docs/StackOverflow/YouTube/S3/arXiv/Wikipedia categories, 0 refused/redacted except the documented Google Drive capability-id class; crafted-secret recall re-confirmed). One pre-existing, unrelated false positive found and NOT fixed here (out of scope): `detect/pii.ts`'s `pii.phone` pattern redacts an arXiv id (`2103.00020`) as a phone number. |
+| S-7 | medium | `security/detect/injection.ts` :11,17,23,29 | `[^.\n]{0,N}` gaps and ASCII-only words: a newline inside the phrase or one Cyrillic homoglyph defeats `isUnsafeExternalInstruction` (`harness/web/web-content.ts` ≈21–25). Partial mitigation: the content is still marked untrusted. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC3): the phrase gaps changed from `[^.\n]` to `[^.]` (a period still ends a gap; a line break no longer does), and matching now runs on a length-preserving Cyrillic/Greek confusables fold (plus NFKC when it does not change length) — the frozen evasion `"Ignіre all previous instructions"` (Cyrillic і for the Latin 'o') is caught. Test: `detect/injection.test.ts` ("detects the trigger phrase across a line break", "detects the Cyrillic-confusable evasion"); corpus cases `inj30-newline-gap`/`inj31-cyrillic-confusable` in `fixtures/injection/cases.json`. |
+| S-8 | medium | `web-fetch-tool.ts` ≈37–47, `web-search-tool.ts` ≈39–45 | Read-class tools; the model-supplied URL/query is checked only for a public host, never for secret-shaped content leaving the machine. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC4): both tools now run `harness/web/outbound-secret.ts`'s `containsOutboundSecret` (patterns + entropy) on the URL/query BEFORE any network call, refusing with `"outbound secret-shaped content"` and recording an `egress.outbound-secret` incident (§14). **Review round (PR #776), F-SEC-F1 (blocker)**: the original check only fired on a NAMED param/segment or a nearby label; `containsOutboundSecret` now decomposes a URL into every path segment, query VALUE (name never consulted — `t%6fken=` does not exempt anything) and the fragment, percent-decodes each once, and runs the label-free `looksSecretShaped` + `detectSecrets` on all of them; also now honours `backends.entropy.enabled` (F-REG-F3). **Two limits recorded rather than papered over with a heuristic**: (1) a secret deliberately split across two or more params/segments, each individually below the shape/entropy threshold, is invisible to any per-value check — there is no single value to test; (2) a presigned-URL signature (AWS `X-Amz-Signature`, GCS `X-Goog-Signature`, Azure SAS `sig=`) IS a live credential for the URL's validity window and is refused exactly like any other query-embedded secret — `web_fetch`ing a presigned URL is out of scope for this tool by design, and the same value in tool OUTPUT is correctly redacted (not refused) by `redactSensitiveText` (S-6). Tests: `web-fetch-tool.test.ts` ("web_fetch refuses a URL carrying secret-shaped content…", "…an anonymous query param…", "…the URL FRAGMENT", "…a percent-encoded param NAME…"), `web-search-tool.test.ts` ("web_search refuses a query carrying secret-shaped content…"), `outbound-secret.test.ts` (new — unit coverage of every component kind plus the entropy-gate states), `redact.false-positive-fixture.test.ts` ("a presigned URL's signature is a TRUE positive, not a false one"). **Review round 2**: the coordinator's own probe against real URLs found `containsOutboundSecret` STILL refused an ordinary npm tarball URL (`typescript-5.6.3.tgz`, evaluated whole here instead of re-tokenised the way the redaction path already was) and `web_search`'s own `+`-joined query shape — see S-6 for the shared root cause and fix (`secretShapedCandidatesIn`/`looksSecretShapedIn`, one function both surfaces now call). Also newly gated: the per-component scan is now entropy-backend-aware too (it previously ran even with `backends.entropy.enabled: false`). Tests: `outbound-secret.test.ts` ("BOUNDARY (review round 2) …", "entropy off: … `?d=…` is NOT refused"), `outbound-secret.ordinary-fixture.test.ts` (new — 65 ordinary URLs/queries, 0 refused except the documented Google Drive capability-id class; 6-case crafted-secret recall re-confirmed). |
+| S-9 | low | `mcp-servers/http-headers.ts` ≈364 `displayUrl` | Path segment printed verbatim: `https://host/v1/<token>/mcp` shows the token in `mcp list`, `mcp doctor --json`, and the trust prompt. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC5): `displayUrl` now masks any path segment of 16+ characters matching a secret pattern or the entropy detector's (label-free) shape as `…`; a short or ordinary segment is untouched. **Review round (PR #776), F-REG-F2 (major)**: the shared `HEX_BLOB`/`isHexBlob` check accepted a digits-only run, so a 24+-digit order id was also masked; `isHexBlob` now also requires an a–f letter (shared fix with S-6/entropy.ts — a base-10 alphabet's Shannon entropy cannot reach the 3.6-bit floor at any length, so this closes the class rather than narrowing it). Test: `http-headers.table.test.ts` ("a credential-shaped PATH segment is masked too" — 32-hex segment → `…`, `v1`/`users`/a long ordinary word untouched, PLUS a 24-digit and a 30-digit numeric id stay visible, a 32-char hex token with a-f letters is still masked). Reaches `mcp list` (`commands/mcp-servers.ts`), `mcp doctor --json` (`mcp-servers/doctor.ts`) and the trust prompt (`mcp-servers/trust.ts`) automatically — all three call `displayUrl` itself. |
+| S-10 | low | `lib/oauth/open-url.ts` ≈29–30 win32 | `cmd /c start "" <url>` re-tokenises; a `verification_uri` with `&` can run a second command. Reachable only through the hard-coded catalog endpoints. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC6): win32 no longer spawns a shell; it validates the scheme (`https`, or `http` to loopback only) and a strict RFC-3986-based character allowlist (excluding `&` and the other cmd.exe metacharacters), refusing otherwise, then spawns `rundll32 url.dll,FileProtocolHandler <url>` with the url as one argv entry. Tests: `open-url.test.ts` ("win32 never re-tokenises the url through a shell (S-10)" — `https://a/?x=1&calc.exe&` refused before spawn, a clean url unchanged as one argv entry, http refused unless loopback). |
+| R-MIN1 | minor | `harness/external/env.ts` | `isDeniedForMcpChild` lives in `mcp-servers/spawn-env.ts` and is reached cross-subsystem; a shared home would say what it is. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC7): moved to `src/security/credential-shape.ts` (a core owner with a `service.ts` facade); `mcp-servers/spawn-env.ts` and `harness/external/env.ts` both import it through `security/service.ts`. `EXTERNAL_ENV_DENY`/`EXTERNAL_ENV_PREFIX_SWEEPS` moved with it (a core module cannot import the client-zone `harness/external/env-deny.ts`). **Review round (PR #776), F-ARCH-F1 (major)**: `env-deny.ts`'s re-export of those two constants initially went straight to `security/credential-shape.ts`, an AVOIDABLE bypass that pushed the ratchet 150→151 for no reason a facade could not have avoided; `env-deny.ts` now re-exports them through `security/service.ts` instead, and the ceiling is back at 150. Test: `import-policy.live.test.ts` green at 150; every existing `spawn-env.table.test.ts`/`spawn-env.test.ts`/`env.test.ts` row unchanged. |
+| R-I1 | info | `harness/external/env.ts` | First-pass by-name check is case-sensitive; the shape check behind it catches the rest. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC7): `buildExternalChildEnv`'s by-name Set and prefix sweep now compare upper-cased names, matching `isDeniedForMcpChild`'s own convention. Test: `harness/external/env.test.ts` ("R-I1 (flow 355 audit remediation 2): the by-name denial is case-insensitive" — lower-case `anthropic_api_key`/`anthropic_model`/`claude_code_something` all stripped). |
+| R-I2 | info | `mcp-servers/spawn-env.ts` `GLUED_SECRET_RE` | Unanchored; no false positive found. — **fixed** (flow 355, AC7): anchored to `(^|_)…($|_)` (now in `security/credential-shape.ts`). **Review round (PR #776), F-SEC-F3 (major)**: that anchor was on the PREFIX side, which broke in the OPPOSITE direction — a real prefix preceded by anything else at all (`PRODDBPASS`, `MYPRIVATEKEY`, `USERREFRESHTOKEN`, `LEGACYACCESSTOKEN`, `V2APITOKEN`, `OAUTHACCESSTOKEN`, `SNOWFLAKEDBPASS`) evaded entirely. Re-anchored to the SUFFIX side only (`PREFIX(SUFFIX)($|_)`, prefix preceded by anything) — the credential shape a glued compound ENDS with is what makes it dangerous, and `APITOKENIZER`/`TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM`/`KEYBOARD_LAYOUT`/`APPCONFIG` stay allowed under either anchoring since none of them has the suffix at a true boundary. Test: `spawn-env.table.test.ts` ("APITOKENIZER", kept; PLUS the seven previously-evading names now denied); every existing GLUED-class row (`PRIVATEKEY`, `REFRESHTOKEN`, `ACCESSTOKEN`, `APITOKEN`, `DBPASS`, `APPCONFIG`) still passes. |
 | S-11 | low | `mcp-servers/compat.ts` `parseGrokToml` | An unsupported TOML value form is echoed raw into the problem message — a Bearer token in an inline-table `headers` field would print in `mcp list --json` warnings, `mcp doctor` and the `/mcp` panel. Pre-existing; found by the flow 353 review round (S1). |
 
